<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gambaga</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gambaga is a town in the North East Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, on the Gambaga escarpment. It was the early capital of the Mamprugu kingdom before the court moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nalerigu">Nalerigu</a> around 1700, and it remained a trading town on routes to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> lands. In the colonial period it served as an early British administrative centre in the Northern Territories.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gambaga.jpg" alt="Gambaga" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ali.rusuli · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IMG-20190115-WA0049.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
